    "result_text": "The full suite passes with BUILD SUCCESS (2/2 tests, 0 failures). \n\nThe change is complete. Summary of what I did to satisfy the `ownerSegment` spec with minimal structural impact:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `ownerSegment` property to the Owner schema so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **New `OwnerSegments.java`** (small, cohesive helper in the `mapper` package, matching the existing `Localities`/`AgeBands`/`TimeZones` pattern) \u2014 a single static `of(Owner)` that:\n   - computes TIER = `PREMIUM` when the capped `membershipLevel` \u2265 3, else `STANDARD` (reusing `MembershipLevels.levelOf` and the same cap logic the mapper uses for `membershipLevel`);\n   - computes AREA = `METRO` when the locality region (`customerCode` prefix) is NSW/VIC/QLD, else `REGIONAL`.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 one added `@Mapping` line delegating to `OwnerSegments.of(owner)`.\n\nBehaviour is added as a new isolated unit rather than growing any existing method or large class; the only edited method (`toOwnerDto`, an abstract mapper method, CC 1) gained a single line, and no existing helper was touched. Both new acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known region, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown one) pass.",
